  "description": {
    "text": "The Shining Pokémon Poké Ball Gift Box (精灵球礼盒：闪耀宝可梦) is a tin Poké Ball holding one random Shining Pokémon card, one Poké Ball holo card and a 25-card Shining Synergy booster pack, Shower, Supreme or Summon at random. It brought Shining Pokémon cards to the Simplified Chinese game for the first time: Celebi, Genesect, Ho-Oh, Volcanion, Mew, Jirachi, Rayquaza, Lugia and Arceus.\n\nWith luck, a random Pokémon-GX holo took the Poké Ball card's place. These are rainbow Palkia-GX, Mewtwo-GX, Yveltal-GX, Dialga-GX and Xerneas-GX, numbered 011 to 015, past the set's 10. The box was due on 17 February 2023 but was delayed while its packaging was changed, and came out on 17 March.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: The Shining Pokémon Poké Ball Gift Box is coming (3 March 2023)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/product/16330.html"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: Shining Pokémon Poké Ball Gift Box delayed (13 February 2023)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/other/17195.html"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"CSMJC\" mark at the bottom left, and a number out of 010",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokémon China: The Shining Pokémon Poké Ball Gift Box is coming (3 March 2023)",
        "url": "https://www.pokemon.cn/tcg/product/16330.html"
      },
